幕后花絮，还有许多闺蜜的故事。

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.460
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士 6.0》。

9
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:26.790
Hello.
你好。

10
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:27.750
Hi.
嗨。

11
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:28.850
How's it going?
最近怎么样？

12
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.150
It's going so good.
好得不得了。

13
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:30.970
It is?
是吗？

14
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:31.490
Yeah.
对啊。

15
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:32.490
Same.
我也是。

16
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.350
It's just a beautiful day.
今天真是个好日子。

17
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.890
I'm sitting across from my friend, my friend.
我正坐在我的朋友对面，我的朋友。

18
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.550
Oh, that's how I would talk to my kitty cat.
哦，我平时就是这样跟我家小猫说话的。

19
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:40.930
I know.
我知道。

20
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:41.750
You're saying my friend.
你叫我朋友。

21
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.370
And also, we're doing something that's kind of touching my heart this morning.
而且，今天早上我们要做一件挺触动我心的事情。

22
00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:46.390
I'm so excited.
我太激动了。

23
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.650
We're finally doing it.
我们终于要做了。

24
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:47.990
Okay.
好啦。

25
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.210
So, here's what's happening.
那么，情况是这样的。

26
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.710
We are going to break down the paper, Scam Alert, Episode 5.
我们要剖析《纸业公司》的第5集《诈骗警报》。

27
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.930
But first, you guys, we're going to kick things off with an Around the Town.
但首先，各位，我们要以一个“城市周遭”环节来开场。

28
00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:58.670
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

29
00:00:58.930 --> 00:00:59.290
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

30
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.230
This is the segment we've been wanting to do.
这是我们一直想做的环节。

31
00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:06.070
You guys remember, in our breakdown of Episode 2 of the paper, I shared about my grandmother
大家还记得吗，在我们剖析《纸业公司》第2集时，我分享了我外祖母

32
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.370
Lena's hometown newspaper column.
莉娜的家乡报纸专栏。

33
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.390
She would document little slice-of-life moments happening in my hometown of Archer City, Texas.
她会记录下我的家乡德克萨斯州阿彻市的生活点滴。

34
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.370
And we just loved this idea.
我们太喜欢这个主意了。

35
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.730
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

36
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.330
So, we decided to make it part of our show.
所以，我们决定把它做成我们节目的一部分。

37
00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.630
And we asked you all to send in your Around the Town tidbits and moments.
我们邀请大家发来你们的“城市周遭”趣闻和生活片段。

38
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.770
And we're going to start sharing them in these episodes as we continue to break down the paper.
在我们继续剖析《纸业公司》的同时，我们将开始在这些剧集里分享它们。

39
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:33.030
Yeah, and since this is the first one, we thought we'd kick off the episode with it.
对，既然这是第一期，我们觉得用这个来给节目开场最合适。

40
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.090
All right, here we go.
好了，我们开始吧。

41
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.530
Office ladies reporting for Around the Town.
办公室女士“城市周遭”报道组，随时待命。

42
00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:40.630
This one is from Catalina in Newton, Kansas.
这一条来自堪萨斯州牛津市的卡塔利娜。

43
00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.870
And Catalina put her Around the Town in the newsy jargon.
而且卡塔利娜用新闻式的行话写了她的“城市周遭”。

44
00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.030
Oh, I love it.
哦，我太喜欢了。

45
00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.970
Like the way your grandma wrote them.
就像你外祖母写的那种风格。

46
00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.990
Here is what she said.
她是这么说的。

47
00:01:49.990 --> 00:02:00.130
Miss Catalina Bergman and her mother, Mrs. Robert Bergman, started the new year with a visit to the Van Gogh Experience in Wichita, followed by Lunch at the Dairy Queen.
卡塔利娜·伯格曼小姐和她的母亲罗伯特·伯格曼太太以参观威奇托的梵高体验展开启了新的一年，随后在冰雪皇后的DQ餐厅用了午餐。

48
00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.230
Lunch at the DQ?
在DQ吃午餐？

49
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.890
I love Lunch at the DQ.
我太喜欢去DQ吃午餐了。

50
00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.270
Me too.
我也是。

51
00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:04.870
Are you kidding?
你开玩笑吧？

52
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:05.690
Not dinner.
不是晚餐。

53
00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:06.470
Lunch.
是午餐。

54
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.350
There's something about eating it at lunch.
午餐吃这个总有一种别样的感觉。

55
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:09.230
Well...
这个嘛……

56
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.030
Why is that?
为什么这么说？

57
00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.050
Why is it better?
为什么这样更好吃？

58
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.170
It's so great.
真的太棒了。

59
00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:12.910
I don't know.
我也不知道。

60
00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.530
I love any of their baskets.
我特别喜欢他们家的各种套餐。

61
00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:21.330
You know, their chicken finger basket and the gravy with the french fries and the toaSt.
你知道的，他们的鸡柳套餐，还有配炸薯条和吐司的肉汁。

62
00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.690
Oh, I know.
哦，我懂的。

63
00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:23.630
All right.
好的。

64
00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.090
Well, next up, this is from Trista N.
那么接下来，这条来自阿尔伯塔省的……

65
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.770
in Alberta, Canada.
加拿大阿尔伯塔省的特里斯坦·N。

66
00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.830
She says, I live in a small town in Alberta, Canada called Morinville.
她说，我住在加拿大阿尔伯塔省一个叫莫林维尔的小镇。

67
00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:40.750
We used to have this beautiful Catholic church that was built in 1907, but unfortunately, it burned down in 2021.
我们以前有一座美丽的天主教堂，建于1907年，但不幸的是，它在2021年被大火烧毁了。

68
00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.070
Before it was burnt down, the church bells used to ring all the time, and it was just such a cozy feeling.
在被烧毁之前，教堂的钟声总是响个不停，那种感觉真的很温馨。

69
00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:54.710
It took some time to rebuild it, and the church bells finally rang once again after almost five years yesterday.
重建它花了一些时间，就在昨天，时隔将近五年，教堂的钟声终于再次敲响了。

70
00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.430
It was such a great feeling to hear them ring again.
再次听到钟声响起，那种感觉真是太棒了。

71
00:02:58.830 --> 00:02:59.290
Wow.
哇。

72
00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.490
Isn't that so special?
这难道不是很特别吗？

73
00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.190
Yeah.
是啊。

74
00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.210
I mean, that's meaningful.
我的意思是，这很有意义。

75
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:03.850
Yeah.
对啊。

76
00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.510
That they rebuilt them and to hear them ring, I mean...
他们重建了教堂，还能听到钟声敲响，我是说……

77
00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.350
Throughout the town.
响彻整个小镇。

78
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:15.150
It just feels like such a, I don't know, very poetic, symbolic of, you know, rebuilding.
就让人觉得，怎么说呢，非常富有诗意，象征着，你懂的，重建。

79
00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:15.890
Rebuilding.
重建。

80
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:16.630
Yeah.
是啊。

81
00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:17.710
All right.
好吧。

82
00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.590
Elizabeth P.
伊丽莎白·P.

83
00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.210
from Bellingham, Washington said,
来自华盛顿州贝灵厄姆，她说，

84
00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.170
So, we have a lot of large, tall trees along the freeway up here.
所以，我们这里的公路沿线有许多又大又高的树。

85
00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:32.930
Someone put a giant sloth way up in one of the trees, and you could see it from the freeway as you drive north.
有人在高高的树上挂了一只巨大的树懒，你开车往北走时从公路上就能看到它。

86
00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.650
Well, the Washington State Department of Transportation took it down.
结果，华盛顿州交通运输部把它给取下来了。

87
00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:43.470
But that did not dissuade the good people of Bellingham from bringing the sloth spirit back.
但这并没有打消贝灵厄姆好心市民们重燃树懒精神的念头。

88
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:50.150
After several back and forths of the sloth going up and WSDOT taking it down,
经过好几个回合的树懒被挂上去、华盛顿州交通运输部又把它取下来的拉锯战之后，

89
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:57.450
the mystery sloth person somehow managed to get the sloth to new heights so that it could not be brought down.
这位神秘的树懒达人居然设法把树懒送到了更高的高度，让人再也够不着把它取下来。

90
00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:07.430
So, slothy has been up there ever since and has a spotlight lit up on him somehow at night for all to easily see him from the freeway.
所以，树懒从小到大一直都在那儿，不知怎么的，晚上还给它打了一束聚光灯，让大家在公路上能轻而易举地看到它。

91
00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.650
Slothy lives on.
树懒永存。

92
00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.950
That is so amazing to me.
这对我来说太不可思议了。

93
00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:17.010
It's kind of great that, I guess, the Washington State Department of Transportation was like,
我觉得挺棒的，华盛顿州交通运输部大概觉得，

94
00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:23.130
well, it's high enough up now, it's safe, they love it, clearly, it has its own spotlight, we're leaving it.
好吧，现在挂得够高了，很安全，而且大家显然都很喜欢它，还有它自己的聚光灯，我们就由它去吧。

95
00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.530
I guess so.
我想也是吧。

96
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.130
I want to drive by it.
真想开车去从它旁边路过。

97
00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.750
Well, thank you guys all so much for writing in your Around the Towns.
好吧，非常感谢大家写信分享你们的“城市周遭”故事。

98
00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.730
We'll keep sharing these as the weeks go by.
随着时间的推移，我们会继续分享这些内容。

99
00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.930
Yeah, you can find the folder to share on officeladies.com Around the Town.
对，你们可以在 officeladies.com 的“城市周遭”板块找到分享文件夹。

100
00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.910
I feel like my grandmother would be so proud.
我觉得我奶奶要是知道了会觉得特别骄傲。

101
00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:43.950
Well, now it is time for our chit-chat question of the week, and it's coming from Amy H.
好了，现在是我们每周的闲聊问答时间，这个问题来自加利福尼亚州圣克拉里塔的艾米·H。

102
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.790
in Santa Clarita, California.
加利福尼亚州圣克拉里塔。

103
00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.350
I might have had a hand in selecting this one.
我可能参与挑选了这个问题。

104
00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:48.890
You did.
确实有。

105
00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.650
Hi, I've been a faithful listener since day one and absolutely loved the show.
嗨，我从第一天起就是忠实听众，而且超级喜欢这个节目。

106
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.030
I used to be up in the middle of the night pumping for my baby girl,
我过去常常在半夜醒来给宝贝女儿吸奶，

107
00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:01.690
and I would listen to The Office Ladies or re-watch an episode of The Office.
那时我会听《办公室女士》或者重温一集《办公室》。

108
00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:07.330
It honestly brought me so much joy during postpartum and through COVID, so thank you so much for that.
在产后和疫情期间，它真的带给我数不清的快乐，非常感谢你们。

109
00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:10.930
Jenna and Sam, you mentioned that you both lift weights.
珍娜和萨姆，你们提到过你们两个都举重。

110
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.650
What do your workouts usually look like?
你们平时的锻炼通常是怎样的？

111
00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.750
Thanks again for all your laughs and heart you've put into the show.
再次感谢你们为节目付出的欢笑和用心。

112
00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.330
You all feel like friends at this point.
到这个时候，你们感觉就像朋友一样。

113
00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.490
Oh, Amy, Amy, Amy.
哦，艾米，艾米，艾米。

114
00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.890
I love to talk about weightlifting.
我可太喜欢聊举重了。

115
00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.050
You do.
你确实喜欢。

116
00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.610
You get real sort of, I don't know, like that perky face.
你就会变得有点，我不知道，就像那种神采奕奕的样子。

117
00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:28.890
Perky face?
神采奕奕？

118
00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:29.690
Perky face.
神采奕奕。

119
00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.270
I would love to give an update on my weightlifting.
我很乐意分享一下我最近举重的进展。

120
00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.770
I have been weightlifting for over a year now,
我开始举重已经有一年多了，

121
00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.770
and I am so passionate about it.
而且我对它充满了热情。

122
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.810
I weightlift with Body Fit by Amy.
我跟着艾米的身体塑形（Body Fit by Amy）进行举重训练。

123
00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.990
You're inspiring me that 2026 is going to be the year I weightlift because of you.
因为你，你让我觉得2026年将是我开始举重的一年。

124
00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:45.690
Really?
真的吗？

125
00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:46.210
Yes.
是的。

126
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.450
I am so excited.
我太兴奋了。

127
00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.370
You say that.
你嘴上这么说。

128
00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.290
You leave me such great messages about it,
你为此给我留了好多超棒的语音消息，

129
00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.810
and it makes you feel so empowered.
而且它会让你觉得充满了力量。

130
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.510
I'm like, I want to get on this train.
我就想，我也要搭上这班车。

131
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:58.750
Listen, after breaking my shoulder and all that cancer treatment,
听着，在经历骨折和所有那些癌症治疗之后，

132
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:05.250
I am stronger physically than I've ever been in my life because I used to work out,
我身体的强壮程度达到了我人生的巅峰，因为我以前也锻炼过，

133
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.190
but my workouts were always, I mean, if I'm being honest,
但我的锻炼总是——说实话的话，

134
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:15.590
they were all geared toward burning calories, losing weight, maintaining weight.
它们全都是为了燃烧卡路里、减肥、维持体重。

135
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.450
But the weightlifting is about something else.
但举重则完全是另一回事。

136
00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.210
It's about being physically strong and capable in my body.
它关乎让我的身体变得强壮且充满力量。

137
00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:28.850
And for me, it's also about, you know, making me have less side effects from my medications
对我来说，它还关乎，你知道的，减少药物带来的副作用，

138
00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.310
because it's been proven that that really helps.
因为事实证明这真的很有帮助。

139
00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.690
And I'm like, I can't say enough great things about it.
所以我总是觉得，我对它的赞美简直无以复加。

140
00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.250
I love it.
我太爱它了。

141
00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.910
And I want to say, I have been lifting weights for over a year
而且我想说，我举重已经一年多了，

142
00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.570
with no change on the number to the scale.
体重秤上的数字一点都没变。

143
00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.850
This is really about strength.
这真的完全关乎力量。

144
00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.630
This is really about, like, being capable.
这真的完全关乎，比如说，变得更有能力。

145
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:48.670
Yeah.
对。

146
00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:52.350
But I have lost an inch and a half in my waiSt.
但我的腰围减了整整一寸半。

147
00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.050
Hey!
嘿！

148
00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:53.870
Yeah.
对。

149
00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.910
So it's like, things are, like, reforming.
所以就像是，身体在进行重塑。

150
00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:57.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

151
00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:58.770
You're like a transformer.
你就像个变形金刚。

152
00:06:58.990 --> 00:06:59.590
A little bit.
有点像。

153
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.370
A little box in disguise.
伪装的小盒子。

154
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.370
Sam, what about you?
山姆，你呢？

155
00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.070
Are you, you're still weightlifting, right?
你还在举重，对吧？

156
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.650
Yeah, still weightlifting, yeah.
对，还在举重，对。

157
00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.130
So I've been doing CrossFit is what I've been doing.
所以我现在在练的是CrossFit综合体能训练。

158
00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.050
