什么互联网？

641
00:25:32.390 --> 00:25:33.190
What part of the internet are you on?
你到底在上网的哪个角落？

642
00:25:33.190 --> 00:25:34.570
I hooked up with a guy.
我和一个家伙好上了。

643
00:25:35.290 --> 00:25:38.330
He was a hot dog, and we did the little corn on the cob.
他是个热狗，然后我们搞了点带芯玉米棒那一套。

644
00:25:38.570 --> 00:25:38.930
Yes.
没错。

645
00:25:39.210 --> 00:25:40.150
You could say that.
你可以这么说。

646
00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:44.610
I would know that he was circumcised, and you had sex with your clothes on.
那我就会知道他是没割包皮的，而且你们穿着衣服做了爱。

647
00:25:44.650 --> 00:25:44.730
Uncircumcised?
没割包皮？

648
00:25:44.990 --> 00:25:45.390
No, no.
不，不。

649
00:25:45.530 --> 00:25:47.650
Hot dog in a bun means uncircumcised.
夹在面包里的热狗意思是没割包皮。

650
00:25:47.730 --> 00:25:48.870
If it's still in the bun.
如果它还在面包里的话。

651
00:25:48.970 --> 00:25:50.070
Oh, right, right, right, right.
哦，对，对，对，对。

652
00:25:50.090 --> 00:25:51.590
Just a hot dog.
就一个热狗。

653
00:25:51.590 --> 00:25:57.090
Okay, I had a hot dog with a bun and some—while we were corn on the cob.
好吧，我吃了一个热狗加热狗面包还有一些——在我们吃玉米棒子的时候。

654
00:25:57.470 --> 00:25:57.850
Yes.
是的。

655
00:25:59.010 --> 00:26:00.210
Sounds great.
听起来不错。

656
00:26:00.610 --> 00:26:01.450
All right.
好的。

657
00:26:02.090 --> 00:26:04.910
Well, everyone, you can start listening with your kids again.
好了，各位，你们可以带上孩子重新开始收听了。

658
00:26:05.730 --> 00:26:09.830
Esmeralda is going to leave this meeting and go in her office and shut her door.
埃斯梅拉达要离开这个会议室，进她自己的办公室并关上门。

659
00:26:10.010 --> 00:26:11.110
She rushes out.
她冲了出去。

660
00:26:11.210 --> 00:26:13.290
Yeah, and everybody clocks it.
对，大家都注意到了。

661
00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:16.170
Everyone knows that she's being catfished.
大家都知道她被网络交友诈骗了。

662
00:26:16.350 --> 00:26:16.490
Yeah.
是啊。

663
00:26:17.030 --> 00:26:20.470
Nicole and Adalola are incredibly happy about this.
妮可和阿达洛拉对此感到高兴得无以复加。

664
00:26:20.470 --> 00:26:25.710
They are sick and tired of Esmeralda, and they're delighted.
她们对埃斯梅拉达早就厌烦透顶，此刻幸灾乐祸。

665
00:26:26.830 --> 00:26:32.050
Nicole has a talking head where she lists off this beef she's had with Esmeralda for a long time.
妮可有一个单独采访镜头，细数了她和埃斯梅拉达积怨已久的旧账。

666
00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:40.690
Well, Ned is so excited when he realizes, oh, my gosh, we have someone on the inside who has dealt with the catfisher.
内德一意识到“天哪，我们居然内线有人，这人还跟那个骗子打过交道”，整个人兴奋得不行。

667
00:26:40.890 --> 00:26:43.110
We got to get her to tell her story.
我们得让她把故事讲出来。

668
00:26:43.550 --> 00:26:45.930
He wants it to be a six-part series.
他想把它做成一个六集的系列节目。

669
00:26:46.130 --> 00:26:47.790
He thinks it could be award-winning.
他觉得这能拿奖。

670
00:26:47.790 --> 00:26:52.630
He's very excited about this possible news-breaking article that he can write.
他对这篇可能轰动一时的独家报道感到非常兴奋。

671
00:26:53.330 --> 00:26:54.870
Kimberly now is going to come in.
金伯利现在要进来了。

672
00:26:55.010 --> 00:26:59.310
She's pissed off because they have her whiteboard, and she's going to pull the F out.
她气冲冲的，因为他们拿了她的白板，她要发飙了。

673
00:26:59.550 --> 00:26:59.830
Yes.
是的。

674
00:26:59.990 --> 00:27:01.890
Kimberly, played by writer Mo Welch.
金伯利，由编剧莫·韦尔奇饰演。

675
00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:05.030
I got very obsessed with her sweater.
我迷上了她的毛衣。

676
00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:13.510
Did you notice at 5 minutes, 29 seconds, she's wearing this, like, black short sleeve, and there's a small little gray sheep on her left shoulder.
你有没有注意到在5分29秒的时候，她穿着一件黑色的短袖，左肩上有一只灰色的小绵羊。

677
00:27:13.910 --> 00:27:15.050
Did you clock that?
你注意到了吗？

678
00:27:15.170 --> 00:27:17.090
I had to take a screen grab of it.
我不得不截了个图。

679
00:27:17.190 --> 00:27:17.910
Is it a brand?
这是什么牌子吗？

680
00:27:18.170 --> 00:27:19.430
I wanted to know.
我很想知道。

681
00:27:19.590 --> 00:27:22.590
I Googled, where can I buy this shirt with one sheep?
我谷歌了一下“在哪能买到这件有一只绵羊的衬衫”。

682
00:27:22.750 --> 00:27:23.570
You can't.
根本买不到。

683
00:27:23.730 --> 00:27:25.210
You get lots of sheep.
你只能买到成群的绵羊。

684
00:27:25.410 --> 00:27:26.630
You get a black sheep.
你能买到黑羊。

685
00:27:26.630 --> 00:27:28.570
No one gray sheep.
就是没有单只灰羊。

686
00:27:28.850 --> 00:27:32.030
So I reached out to the costume designer for the paper.
所以我联系了该剧的服装设计师。

687
00:27:32.210 --> 00:27:32.530
Oh!
哦！

688
00:27:32.910 --> 00:27:34.230
Kathleen Felix Hager.
凯瑟琳·费利克斯·黑格。

689
00:27:34.530 --> 00:27:36.290
Her resume is so impressive.
她的简历太牛了。

690
00:27:36.610 --> 00:27:43.010
She has done the costume design for Hacks, Veep, Space Force, Dexter, so many other shows.
她担任过《绝望hacks》、《副总统》、《太空部队》、《嗜血法医》等好多节目的服装设计。

691
00:27:43.010 --> 00:27:48.970
And I said, Kathleen, can you please tell me about this little gray sheep t-shirt?
然后我说，凯瑟琳，你能跟我讲讲这件灰色小绵羊T恤吗？

692
00:27:49.270 --> 00:27:57.790
And she said, first of all, I want to share that Greg and Michael really let me have fun with the characters, and the cast is so lovely and amazing to work with.
她说，首先，我想分享的是，格雷格和迈克尔真的很放手让我为角色进行创作，而且演员阵容非常可爱，合作起来太棒了。

693
00:27:58.090 --> 00:28:04.570
As far as the sheep sweater, that sheep is actually the logo for the Softies company.
至于那件绵羊毛衣，那只羊其实是“软心”公司的标志。

694
00:28:05.530 --> 00:28:08.130
Oh, so she had to design that.
哦，所以那是她自己设计的。

695
00:28:08.130 --> 00:28:17.830
She made various sweatshirts and polos for all the Softies employees and a special purple jumpsuit just for Kimberly to wear with the sheep logo embroideried on it.
她为所有“软心”公司的员工制作了各种运动衫和Polo衫，还专门为金伯利定制了一件紫色连体裤，上面绣着绵羊的标志。

696
00:28:18.070 --> 00:28:23.050
And then I was like, well, Kathleen, while I have you, can you share with me about any of the other characters?
然后我就想，好吧，凯瑟琳，趁你现在有空，能跟我聊聊其他角色吗？

697
00:28:23.210 --> 00:28:24.590
They have such specific looks.
他们的造型都太有特点了。

698
00:28:24.790 --> 00:28:27.090
For example, Mare has all these cardigans.
比如，梅尔总是穿着各种开衫。

699
00:28:27.250 --> 00:28:29.390
And then, of course, Esmeralda, right?
然后，当然还有埃斯梅拉达，对吧？

700
00:28:29.690 --> 00:28:30.890
Yeah, with her snake belt.
对，她还系着蛇形腰带。

701
00:28:31.050 --> 00:28:31.490
I know.
我知道。

702
00:28:31.490 --> 00:28:39.630
Oh, so she said for Mare, she really leaned into that character's military background, and she has this tomboyish vibe.
哦，所以她说对于玛尔，她真的很契合那个角色的军旅背景，而且她有一种假小子的气质。

703
00:28:39.850 --> 00:28:43.510
She said the sweaters are all vintage, are resale finds.
她说那些毛衣全都是复古款，是在二手店淘来的。

704
00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:47.230
She wanted all of her looks to feel really lived in and real.
她希望她所有的造型都让人觉得很有生活气息而且很真实。

705
00:28:47.370 --> 00:28:47.870
They do.
确实如此。

706
00:28:48.130 --> 00:28:48.950
Isn't that great?
不是很棒吗？

707
00:28:49.070 --> 00:28:49.250
Yeah.
是啊。

708
00:28:49.630 --> 00:28:50.810
She wrote, Esmeralda!
她写道，埃斯梅拉达！

709
00:28:51.650 --> 00:28:53.230
Wow, what can I say?
哇，我能说什么呢？

710
00:28:53.610 --> 00:28:59.610
Sabrina is a whirlwind of energy, and I had so much fun collaborating with her on the creative looks Esmeralda wears.
萨布丽娜就像一阵充满活力的旋风，我和她合作设计埃斯梅拉达穿的那些创意造型时玩得可开心了。

711
00:28:59.610 --> 00:29:07.970
She said Esmeralda has a taste and style of her own, but there is always something a bit off or wrong in a wonderful way.
她说埃斯梅拉达有她自己的品味和风格，但总有一些地方透着那么点古怪或是不对劲，不过这种不对劲妙极了。

712
00:29:08.150 --> 00:29:11.950
I felt like in this episode, it was that butterfly hair clip.
我觉得在这一集里，就是那个蝴蝶发卡。

713
00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:12.850
Really?
真的吗？

714
00:29:13.090 --> 00:29:13.450
Yes.
对。

715
00:29:13.570 --> 00:29:15.990
It was just odd in the right way.
它就是那种恰到好处的怪异。

716
00:29:16.150 --> 00:29:17.290
That red dress is gorgeous.
那件红裙子太美了。

717
00:29:17.550 --> 00:29:17.670
Yeah.
是啊。

718
00:29:17.670 --> 00:29:22.890
And then she wears this gold belt around it, even though it goes over the zipper in the back.
然后她还在外面系了一条金色腰带，哪怕它其实是压在后面的拉链上的。

719
00:29:23.070 --> 00:29:23.330
Yes.
没错。

720
00:29:23.330 --> 00:29:32.770
I did ask her about the belts, and she said the belts were all costume house finds and sourced from vintage and resale, a lot of the real, real online.
我确实问过她关于腰带的事，她说那些腰带都是在服装仓库淘来的，源自复古和二手货，很多都是从The RealReal网购的。

721
00:29:33.110 --> 00:29:34.330
Do you know this, the real, real?
你知道这个吗，The RealReal？

722
00:29:34.490 --> 00:29:35.570
Of course the real, real.
我当然知道The RealReal。

723
00:29:35.850 --> 00:29:35.910
I know.
我知道。

724
00:29:35.910 --> 00:29:37.870
I buy things from the real, real all the time.
我经常在The RealReal上买东西。

725
00:29:38.090 --> 00:29:41.390
And then she said, I also want to share about Ned.
然后她说，我还想分享一下关于内德的事。

726
00:29:42.050 --> 00:29:47.630
Donal is super collaborative, and he loved all the textures and subtle patterns we mixed and matched.
唐纳尔非常喜欢合作，他很喜欢我们混搭的各种质感和微妙的图案。

727
00:29:47.910 --> 00:29:49.710
Did you notice his color palette?
你注意到他的色调了吗？

728
00:29:49.850 --> 00:29:50.450
It's intentional.
这是刻意安排的。

729
00:29:50.450 --> 00:29:53.870
Is it like some olive greens and stuff?
是不是有点像橄榄绿之类的？

730
00:29:54.050 --> 00:29:58.510
She said, we stayed in the blue, gray, and green color palette for all of his looks.
她说，他的所有造型我们都局限在蓝色、灰色和绿色的色调里。

731
00:29:58.710 --> 00:29:58.910
Yeah.
对。

732
00:29:59.350 --> 00:30:08.290
And then I went digging, and I found this great article on Femstella.com, and it's all the outfits and where you can get them all online.
然后我深入挖掘了一下，在Femstella.com上发现了一篇很棒的文章，里面写了所有的服装以及你在网上哪里能买到它们。

733
00:30:08.550 --> 00:30:09.910
It's really a great article.
这真是一篇很棒的文章。

734
00:30:10.050 --> 00:30:10.510
I'll share it.
我会分享出来的。

735
00:30:10.690 --> 00:30:11.270
Oh, great.
哦，太好了。

736
00:30:11.750 --> 00:30:15.450
Well, next up, Ned is going to go in to check on Esmeralda.
那么接下来，内德要进去看看埃斯梅拉达了。

737
00:30:15.450 --> 00:30:21.330
He says, I noticed you had a very strong reaction to the catfish story.
他说，我注意到你对那个网恋骗局的故事反应非常强烈。

738
00:30:21.510 --> 00:30:22.250
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

739
00:30:22.490 --> 00:30:24.110
Esmeralda has the best response.
埃斯梅拉达的反应绝了。

740
00:30:24.390 --> 00:30:26.350
She always has such great one-liners.
她总是能爆出那么精彩的金句。

741
00:30:26.530 --> 00:30:28.750
She said, I react strongly to everything.
她说，我对什么事反应都很强烈。

742
00:30:28.950 --> 00:30:30.930
Life is strong, and I'm a strong woman.
生活很强烈，而我是一个坚强的女人。

743
00:30:31.170 --> 00:30:31.550
I know.
我懂的。

744
00:30:32.130 --> 00:30:40.530
Ned is kind of like trying to get her to talk about this new online love that she has and finds out his name.
内德有点像是在试图让她聊聊她新交的那个网恋对象，并打听出了他的名字。

745
00:30:40.990 --> 00:30:42.410
His name is Jarson.
他的名字叫贾森（Jarson）。

746
00:30:42.410 --> 00:30:44.290
I mean, it's a common American name.
我的意思是，这是一个很常见的美国名字。

747
00:30:44.350 --> 00:30:45.310
Very common, she says.
非常常见，她说。

748
00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:46.890
Jason and Jared combined.
杰森（Jason）和贾里德（Jared）的结合体。

749
00:30:47.350 --> 00:30:54.210
I did want to point out at 5 minutes 49 seconds, there is a plant that is dying on Esmeralda's desk.
我确实想指出，在5分49秒的时候，埃斯梅拉达的桌上有一盆正在枯萎的植物。

750
00:30:54.290 --> 00:30:54.830
There is?
是吗？

751
00:30:54.870 --> 00:30:55.230
Yes.
对。

752
00:30:55.450 --> 00:30:56.650
That's pretty amazing.
挺不可思议的。

753
00:30:57.210 --> 00:30:59.630
By the way, do you know why it's called catfishing?
话说回来，你知道为什么这叫“网上虚假身份欺诈”（catfishing）吗？

754
00:31:00.090 --> 00:31:00.710
I don't.
我不知道。

755
00:31:00.810 --> 00:31:02.210
Is this another weird term?
这又是哪个奇怪的词吗？

756
00:31:02.710 --> 00:31:03.190
No.
不是。

757
00:31:03.190 --> 00:31:10.610
So, this thing where you go online and you end up being scammed by someone who's pretending to be somebody they're not,
所以，当你上网时，最终被一个假冒他人身份的人给骗了，

758
00:31:10.790 --> 00:31:17.170
it ended up being called catfishing because there was a 2010 documentary called Catfish.
这种现象被称为catfishing，是因为2010年有一部名为《中邪》的纪录片。

759
00:31:17.410 --> 00:31:18.470
I saw catfish.
我看过《中邪》。'

760
00:31:18.470 --> 00:31:18.650
Yeah.
对。

761
00:31:18.650 --> 00:31:19.650
It was so good.
太棒了。

762
00:31:19.710 --> 00:31:20.590
It's so good.
真的很好看。

763
00:31:20.790 --> 00:31:22.250
Like, watch this documentary.
去看这部纪录片吧。

764
00:31:22.250 --> 00:31:23.170
It's incredible.
太不可思议了。

765
00:31:23.170 --> 00:31:33.750
So, in this documentary, they tell this story of how fishermen keep cod active in their tanks after they've been caught by throwing a catfish in there.
在这部纪录片中，他们讲述了一个故事：渔民在捕到鳕鱼后，把一只鲶鱼扔进鱼槽里，以此来保持鳕鱼的活力。

766
00:31:33.750 --> 00:31:41.610
Because what they were finding was, like, if you just try to transport the cod in a barrel or whatever you transport them in, I don't know, in my mind,
因为他们发现，如果你只是把鳕鱼放在木桶里运输，或者随便什么容器里，我也不知道，在我脑海里，

767
00:31:41.610 --> 00:31:44.990
it's a wooden barrel like the olden days, they're just lazy.
就像老电影里的木桶那样，它们会变得很懒惰。

768
00:31:45.290 --> 00:31:48.890
And then they just sort of, you know, they don't do anything.
然后它们就，你知道的，什么也不做。

769
00:31:48.890 --> 00:31:50.190
And then they don't taste as good.
接着它们的肉就没那么好吃了。

770
00:31:50.370 --> 00:31:52.230
Do they die or something?
它们会死掉还是怎么的？

771
00:31:52.450 --> 00:31:53.730
Does the catfish keep them active?
鲶鱼能让它们保持活力吗？

772
00:31:53.730 --> 00:31:55.170
No, they just get mushy.
不，它们的肉会变得软绵绵的。

773
00:31:55.410 --> 00:31:56.630
They get, like, mushy.
就是那种肉质变烂的感觉。

774
00:31:56.790 --> 00:32:03.110
But if you throw a catfish in the barrel, it keeps them swimming around and active and, like, alert.
但如果你往桶里扔一条鲶鱼，它就会逼得它们四处游动、保持活力，而且很警觉。

775
00:32:03.110 --> 00:32:06.710
And then when they get to shore, the cod is going to taste better.
等它们被运到岸上时，鳕鱼的肉就会更好吃。

776
00:32:06.970 --> 00:32:07.150
Huh.
哼。

777
00:32:07.290 --> 00:32:11.150
So, this guy says, listen, I think this person's a little bit like a catfish.
所以有个家伙说，听着，我觉得这个人有点像鲶鱼。

778
00:32:11.170 --> 00:32:12.730
They're just keeping life interesting.
他们只是在让生活变得有趣。

779
00:32:13.250 --> 00:32:15.390
It's sort of like didn't, like, I don't know.
这有点像……我不知道。

780
00:32:15.550 --> 00:32:18.710
Is it so bad to be a catfish in a bunch of cod?
在一群鳕鱼里当一条鲶鱼，真的有那么坏吗？

781
00:32:19.050 --> 00:32:21.990
And so, that's where the term for the movie came from.
所以，这就是电影片名的由来。

782
00:32:22.270 --> 00:32:23.650
And then it, like, blew up from there.
然后这个词就从那以后彻底火了。

783
